	<FilterPreset ObjectID="9" ClassID="ee52a7d2-069e-47f7-aa30-e3e3286b65a3" Version="3">
		<Description>Place two adjustment layers (for best results, make them 8 frames long) side by side, with the cut between them being on the cut between your clips you want to create the transition over. Add the '1. Main Preset' onto both of those.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;Then create a 3rd adjustment layer above those two just created, which covers both adjustment layers, (if you use 8 frames for each one, then it'll be 16 frames long). Then drag and drop any of the transitions I've created onto the third (longest) adjustment layer.&#13;&#10;&#13;&#10;NOTE: on the ZOOM IN &amp; ZOOM OUT transitions you must delete one of the below adjustment layers. For ZOOM IN, delete the first one. For ZOOM OUT delete the second one.</Description>
		<FilterMatchName>AE.ADBE Geometry2</FilterMatchName>
		<Component ObjectRef="10"/>
		<MediaType>228cda18-3625-4d2d-951e-348879e4ed93</MediaType>
		<AnchorInPoint>914974099200000</AnchorInPoint>
		<AnchorOutPoint>915041836800000</AnchorOutPoint>
		<Speed>1.</Speed>
		<TransitionDuration>0</TransitionDuration>
		<Node Version="1">
		</Node>
		<Type>0</Type>
	</FilterPreset>
